Subject: [PATCH 36/43] Sync the liveness engine: F18 print guards (PAD latch,
 volatility cap)

Engine jars from Mosip26 13e3eae (part2-print-latch: 216b4db "F18:
session print guards in the analyzer"). The analyzer now caps the
score at 0.60 for the rest of a session once a 3-frame median falls
below 0.30 (PAD latch), and while the second-lowest of the last 10
model scores is below 0.85 (volatility cap), so a printed photo can no
longer pass passively on a retry. Both are on by default
(padLatchThreshold, volatilityMinScore; off disables). padDetails:
volatility_cap and pad_latch replace minifas_v2_c2 and
minifas_v1se_spoof (nothing here read them). The models and
CameraXFrameSource.java are unchanged (same SHA-256).

Tests: module tests 95 (unchanged), Flutter liveness tests 84, all
passing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
